{title: Shall We Gather at the River}
{artist: Robert Lowry}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Closing}
{style: Traditional}
{key: C}
{key_original: D}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Shall we gather at the [F]river
Where bright [C]angel feet have [G7]trod
With its [C]crystal tide for[F]ever
Flowing [C]by the [G7]throne of [C]God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Yes, we'll [C]gather at the river
The [F]beautiful, the [C]beautiful river
[C]Gather with the saints at the [F]river
That [C]flows by the [G7]throne of [C]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]On the margin of the [F]river
Washing [C]up its silver [G7]spray
We will [C]talk and worship [F]ever
All the [C]happy [G7]golden [C]day
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Ere we reach the shining [F]river
Lay we [C]every burden [G7]down
Grace our [C]spirits will de[F]liver
And pro[C]vide a [G7]robe and [C]crown
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]At the smiling of the [F]river
Mirror [C]of the Saviour's [G7]face
Saints, whom [C]death will never [F]sever
Lift their [C]songs of [G7]saving [C]grace
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
